    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty strong take lol. but isn't there also an argument that even if we tried to slow it down with laws, the tech itself is just gonna keep developing because of the sheer momentum of R&D and global competition? like, if one country doesn't automate, won't they just get left behind by everyone else who does? isn't that almost a law of physics at this point?",
