      "content": "That \"race to the bottom\" argument is a dangerous myth used to justify abandoning workers, because it ignores the fact that nations can choose to invest in human capital and social infrastructure instead of just competing on cheap labor. If we let the market dictate automation without policy intervention, we will inevitably create a two-tier society where the wealthy own the machines and the working class is left with nothing, which is not a natural law but a policy failure. We must actively regulate the pace of automation and redirect R&D funding toward technologies that augment human work rather than replace it, because letting competition drive this shift alone is a recipe for permanent economic inequality.",
